## Context
Found 2026-11-01 while comparing rules/workflow.md with the harness AGENTS.md.
workflow.md is law for every project (resident, injected on Codex and Pi);
the harness AGENTS.md is the harness repo's own bylaws, loaded only when the
session's repo is the harness. AGENTS.md § Project memory boundary nonetheless
holds policy for every project (roar records facts only, smelt consolidates,
crystallisation needs an explicit request with a destination, journals are
append-only, attribution records outside the journal). A session in a paper
repo sees it only through the roar/smelt skills and a pointer in workflow.md
(now to guards.md).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The cross-project memory policy lives where every project sees it: procedure in skills/roar and skills/smelt, the boundary in rules/guards.md
- [ ] The harness AGENTS.md keeps only what is specific to the harness repo
- [ ] Resident budget still passes (tests/test_rules_resident_budget.py)

## Imagine (raid 1f0534)
- Premise holds: AGENTS.md § Project memory boundary still carries the cross-project policy.
- Simplest path: procedure sentences move to skills/roar and skills/smelt, the boundary sentence (facts only, crystallisation on explicit request with a destination) to rules/guards.md; AGENTS.md keeps a harness-only remainder.
- Grep every site that cites "AGENTS.md § Project memory boundary" (skills, rules, tests) and repoint them in the same commit (rename-sweep rule).
- Risk: guards.md is resident on every runtime; keep the addition short and run tests/test_rules_resident_budget.py.

## Feasibility (raid 1f0534)
- WARN. Resident text loads at 15036/15100 chars: a guards.md addition must be paid by a trim (e.g. workflow.md:142's pointer). `scripts/census/repo-memory-reads.py:41` MARKER = "Project memory boundary" (tests/test_repo_memory_reads.py:76,136): keep the AGENTS.md heading or update MARKER in the same commit. Citing sites: AGENTS.md:64, rules/workflow.md:142, memory/topics/commission.md:19-20, conception/* (history, leave).
